= MediaWiki primitives =

BITwiki V2 is built on MediaWiki's actual primitives rather than a simulated directory structure.

== Core units ==
; Page
: A durable MediaWiki knowledge entry.

; Namespace
: A page class with system meaning, permissions, behavior, or editorial purpose.

; Category
: A grouping mechanism that also produces automatic indexes of member pages.

; Template
: Reusable wikicode or content transcluded into other pages.

; Module
: Reusable program logic, typically Lua through Scribunto.

; Redirect
: A continuity mechanism for aliases, renames, and terminology changes.

; Talk page
: Discussion associated with a page or namespace object.

; Revision
: A saved version of a page.

; History
: The ordered revision record of a page.

; Diff
: A comparison between revisions.

; Special page
: A software-generated operational/query surface; Special pages are not ordinary content files.

== Semantic MediaWiki units ==
; Property
: A typed attribute or relationship attached to semantic content.

; Concept
: A stored semantic query that defines a computed collection.

== Rule ==
V2 should express a requirement with an existing native primitive whenever that primitive already has the correct semantics. New abstractions are justified only when the native model cannot represent the requirement cleanly.

